<section class="section conduct-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="text-center" style="margin-bottom:3rem">
      <span class="section-label">Our Commitment</span>
      <h1 class="section-heading">Code of Conduct</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="conduct-content">
      <p>
        Deccan Queen on Rails is dedicated to providing a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of gender, gender identity, age, sexual orientation, disability, physical appearance, race, ethnicity, nationality, religion, or experience level. We do not tolerate harassment of participants in any form.
      </p>
      <p>
        All attendees, speakers, sponsors, and volunteers are required to follow this Code of Conduct. Violations may result in removal from the conference without refund.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Standards</h2>
      <p>
        We generally assume attendees are thoughtful and well-intentioned, so we don't like being heavy-handed. That said, we take harassment seriously — it has no place at our conference or anywhere else, and it runs counter to both our values as a community and as individuals.
      </p>
      <p>
        A diverse community built on mutual respect is what makes an event like this worthwhile. All communication — in talks, hallway conversations, sponsor booths, or online — should be appropriate for a professional audience representing many different backgrounds.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Consider Unacceptable Behaviour</h2>
      <p>This includes, but isn't limited to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Excessive swearing or abusive language</li>
        <li>Deliberately disrupting talks or sessions</li>
        <li>Offensive comments, jokes, or insults related to gender, sexual orientation, disability, appearance, body size, ethnicity, or cultural background</li>
        <li>Sharing sexually explicit, violent, or discriminatory material in talks or public spaces</li>
        <li>Sharing or threatening to share someone's private information without consent</li>
        <li>Unwelcome physical contact or sexual attention</li>
        <li>Threats, intimidation, stalking, or unwanted photography/recording of individuals</li>
        <li>Repeated harassment of any kind, or encouraging others to do the above</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Sponsors and exhibitors are held to the same standard — booth material, staff attire, and conduct should never be sexualized or discriminatory.
      </p>
      <p>
        Attendees are also expected to follow venue rules; any damage or violation of venue policy may be handled directly by the venue, separately from the conference organizers.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reported incidents may lead to a range of responses — from a warning to immediate removal from the conference without refund — at the organizers' discretion.
      </p>

      <h2>If You Experience or Witness a Violation</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>If you feel safe doing so, let the person know their behaviour is inappropriate and unwelcome.</li>
        <li>You're not obligated to engage further beyond that.</li>
        <li>Report the incident to an organizer as soon as possible — either in person or via the contact details below.</li>
        <li>Where possible, share details of the incident with organizers in writing.</li>
        <li>Please hold off on posting about the incident publicly until organizers have had a chance to address it.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Report a Violation</h2>
      <p>
        To report a violation,
        email <a href="mailto:hello@deccanqueenonrails.com">hello@deccanqueenonrails.com</a>, <br />
        call <a href="tel:+917820878393">+91 78208 78393</a>,
        or find any organizer on-site.
      </p>

      <p>
        Thank you for helping make Deccan Queen on Rails a welcoming, respectful event for everyone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
